msgid ""
"Decides how to interpret the <em>Crop left</em> and <em>Crop right</em> "
"values.<br>\n"
"    \tNote: for the horizontal type, absolute values are the longitude (for "
"the location\n"
"source type) and time (in milliseconds since epoch) for the rest of the data "
"source types)"
msgstr ""
"<![CDATA[Nosaka, kā interpretēt <em>kadrēt kreiso pusi</em> un <em>kadrēt "
"labo pusi</em> vērtības.<br>\n"
"    \tIevērībai: horizontālam tipam absolūtās vērtības ir garums (atrašanās "
"vietas\n"
"avota tipam) un laiks (milisekundēs kopš epoha) visiem pārējiem datu avotu "
"tipiem)]]>"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/gpsgraphic.xml
#: rc.cpp:1176 rc.cpp:1190
#, kde-format
msgid "Percentage from min..max,Absolute value"
msgstr "Procentuāli no min..maks.,Absolūtā vērtība"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/gpsgraphic.xml
#: rc.cpp:1178
#, kde-format
msgid "Crop left"
msgstr "Kadrēt kreiso pusi"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/gpsgraphic.xml
#: rc.cpp:1180
#, fuzzy, kde-format
#| msgid ""
#| "<![CDATA[Crops data from the left side of the graph (effectively zooming "
#| "in). <br>\n"
#| "    \tThe value is interpreted either as a percentage of total or an "
#| "absolute value depending on crop_mode_h. In percentage mode, the values "
#| "are not restricted to 0-100 to allow for \"zoom out\" behaviour (ie: "
#| "cropping -50 left will add an extra half of the total horizontal "
#| "distance). Values over 100 (in % mode) will effectively not display "
#| "anything. If <em>Graph Type</em> is set to <b>Speedometer</b>, all crop "
#| "left/right values are ignored.]]>"
msgid ""
"Crops data from the left side of the graph (effectively zooming in). <br>\n"
"    \tThe value is interpreted either as a percentage of total or an "
"absolute value depending on crop_mode_h. In percentage mode, the values are "
"not restricted to 0-100 to allow for \"zoom out\" behaviour (ie: cropping "
"-50 left will add an extra half of the total horizontal distance). Values "
"over 100 (in % mode) will effectively not display anything. If <em>Graph "
"Type</em> is set to <b>Speedometer</b>, all crop left/right values are "
"ignored."
msgstr ""
"<![CDATA[Kadrē datus no grafika kreisās puses (proti, tuvina). <br>\n"
"    \tVērtību programma interpretē kā procentuālu izteiksmi no atkarībā no "
"kopējās vai absolūtās vērtības atkarībā no „crop_mode_h“. Procentuālajā "
"režīmā vērtības nav ierobežotas staro 0—100, tāpēc ir iespējama arī "
"tālināšana (proti, kadrējot -50 no kreisās puses pievienos papildu pusi "
"kopējam horizontālajam attālumam). Vērtības, kas pārsniedz 100 (procentu "
"režīmā) neko neparādīs. Ja <em>grafika tips</em> ir <b>spidometrs</b>, visas "
"kadrējuma kreisās/labās vērtības tiks ignorētas.]]>"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/gpsgraphic.xml
#: rc.cpp:1182
#, kde-format
msgid "Crop right"
msgstr "Kadrēt labo pusi"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/gpsgraphic.xml
#: rc.cpp:1184
#, fuzzy, kde-format
#| msgid ""
#| "<![CDATA[Same as <em>Crop left</em> but for the right side, and "
#| "percentage type is interpreted as an inverse percentage (ie: 100 = do not "
#| "crop anything). Values under 0 will effectively not display anything.]]>"
msgid ""
"Same as <em>Crop left</em> but for the right side, and percentage type is "
"interpreted as an inverse percentage (ie: 100 = do not crop anything). "
"Values under 0 will effectively not display anything."
msgstr ""
"<![CDATA[Tas pats, kas <em>kadrēt pa kreisi</em>, bet labajai pusei. "
"Procentuālo tipu programma interpretē kā apgrieztu procentuālu vērtību "
"(proti, 100 neko nekadrēs). Vērtības zem 0 neko neparādīs.]]>"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/gpsgraphic.xml
#: rc.cpp:1186
#, kde-format
msgid "Crop mode vertical"
msgstr "Vertikālās kadrēšanas režīms"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/gpsgraphic.xml
#: rc.cpp:1188
#, fuzzy, kde-format
#| msgid ""
#| "<![CDATA[Decides how to interpret the <em>Crop bottom</em> and <em>Crop "
#| "top</em> values.<br/>\n"
#| "    \tWith an absolute value, it can zoom in to between 100 and 150m of "
#| "altitude to show\n"
#| "small changes in altitude between those 2 values better.<br/>\n"
#| "Note: for the vertical type, absolute values are latitude degrees (for "
#| "the location\n"
#| "source type) and altitude, heart rate, speed for the others interpreted "
#| "as the <em>Legend unit</em>\n"
#| "type where applicable (ie: a value of 10 for altitude will be considered "
#| "meters by default\n"
#| "but if changing <em>Legend unit</em> to feet it will mean 10 feet).]]>"
msgid ""
"Decides how to interpret the <em>Crop bottom</em> and <em>Crop top</em> "
"values.<br/>\n"
"    \tWith an absolute value, it can zoom in to between 100 and 150m of "
"altitude to show\n"
"small changes in altitude between those 2 values better.<br/>\n"
"Note: for the vertical type, absolute values are latitude degrees (for the "
"location\n"
"source type) and altitude, heart rate, speed for the others interpreted as "
"the <em>Legend unit</em>\n"
"type where applicable (ie: a value of 10 for altitude will be considered "
"meters by default\n"
"but if changing <em>Legend unit</em> to feet it will mean 10 feet)."
msgstr ""
"<![CDATA[Nosaka, kā interpretēt <em>kadrēt apakšu</em> un <em>kadrēt augšu</"
"em> vērtības.<br/>\n"
"    \tAr absolūtu vērtību varat tuvināt starp 100 un 150 m augstuma, lai "
"labāk parādītu\n"
"mazas augstuma izmaiņās starp šīm divām vērtībām.<br/>\n"
"Ievērībai: vertikālajam tipam absolūtās vērtības ir platuma grādi (atrašanās "
"vietas\n"
"avota tipam) un augstums, sirds ritms, ātrums citiem, kas ir parādīts kā "
"<em>apzīmējumu mērvienības</em>\n"
"tips, kur pieejams (proti, augstuma vērtību 10 programma pēc noklusējuma "
"uzskatīs par 10 metriem,\n"
"bet, izmainot <em>apzīmējumu mērvienības</em> uz pēdām, tas nozīmēs 10 "
"pēdu).]]>"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/gpsgraphic.xml
#: rc.cpp:1192
#, kde-format
msgid "Crop bottom"
msgstr "Kadrēt apakšu"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/gpsgraphic.xml
#: rc.cpp:1194
#, fuzzy, kde-format
#| msgid ""
#| "<![CDATA[Crops data from the bottom side of the graph (effectively "
#| "zooming in). <br>\n"
#| "    \tThe value is interpreted either as a percentage of total or an "
#| "absolute value depending on crop_mode_v. In percentage mode the values "
#| "are not restricted to 0-100 to allow for \"zoom out\" behaviour (ie: "
#| "cropping -50 bot will add an extra half of the total vertical distance to "
#| "the bottom). Values over 100 (in % mode) will effectively not display "
#| "anything. If <em>Graph type</em> is <b>Speedometer</b>, this will set the "
#| "minimum needle position which will clamp all values that are lower.]]>"
msgid ""
"Crops data from the bottom side of the graph (effectively zooming in). <br>\n"
"    \tThe value is interpreted either as a percentage of total or an "
"absolute value depending on crop_mode_v. In percentage mode the values are "
"not restricted to 0-100 to allow for \"zoom out\" behaviour (ie: cropping "
"-50 bot will add an extra half of the total vertical distance to the "
"bottom). Values over 100 (in % mode) will effectively not display anything. "
"If <em>Graph type</em> is <b>Speedometer</b>, this will set the minimum "
"needle position which will clamp all values that are lower."
msgstr ""
"<![CDATA[Apgriež datus no grafika apakšas (proti, tuvina). <br>\n"
"    \tVērtību programma interpretē kā procentuālu izteiksmi no kopējā "
"lieluma vai kā absolūtu izteiksmi atkarībā no „crop_mode_v“. Procentuālā "
"režīmā vērtības nav ierobežotas līdz 0—100, kas ļauj arī tālināt (proti, "
"kadrēšana par -50 no apakšas pievienos papildu pusi kopējai vertikālajam "
"attālumam). Vērtības virs 100 (procentuālajā režīmā) nozīmēs, ka nekas "
"netiks parādīts. Ja <em>grafika tips</em> ir <b>spidometrs</b>, šī būs "
"minimālā rādītāja adatas pozīcija, kas nerādīs visas vēl zemākās vērtības.]]>"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/gpsgraphic.xml
#: rc.cpp:1196
#, kde-format
msgid "Crop top"
msgstr "Kadrēt augšu"

#. i18n: file: data/effects/gpsgraphic.xml
#: rc.cpp:1198
#, fuzzy, kde-format
#| msgid ""
#| "<![CDATA[Same as <em>Crop bottom</em> but for the top side, and "
#| "percentage type is interpreted as an inverse percentage (ie: 100 = do not "
#| "crop anything).<br>\n"
#| "    \tValues under 0 will effectively not display anything.]]>"
msgid ""
"Same as <em>Crop bottom</em> but for the top side, and percentage type is "
"interpreted as an inverse percentage (ie: 100 = do not crop anything).<br>\n"
"    \tValues under 0 will effectively not display anything."
msgstr ""
"<![CDATA[Tas pats, kas <em>apgriezt no apakšas</em>, bet apgriež no augšas. "
"Procentuālo tipu programma interpretē kā apgrieztus procentus (proti, 100 = "
"neko neapgriezt).<br>\n"
"    \tVērtības zem 0 neko neparādīs.]]>"

